# What the line gives (ADR-0320 item 7): the script and the standard library
# to read; no network without a +net word, and the roots only with it (INV-0320-4:
# without the word, neither the roots nor a net line in the report).
> grants python3 smoke.py\r
< python3 gets (a POSIX program):
< the terminal
< /bin /usr /etc       read (system)
< \r\n~>
# The same report again, for the negative half: an `x` step looks between the
# last two matches, so they are the report's first line and the prompt.
> grants python3 smoke.py\r
< python3 gets (a POSIX program):
< \r\n~>
x /system/tls
x net:
