# An asyncio HTTPS client against the test PKI's valid server, and the refusal
# of an expired and of a wrong-name certificate before any request byte.
> +net test.zoraya:@TLSVALID@ python3 https_client.py test.zoraya @TLSVALID@\r
< status HTTP/1.1 200
< body Zoraya test page
< \r\n~>
> +net expired.zoraya:@TLSEXPIRED@ python3 https_client.py expired.zoraya @TLSEXPIRED@\r
< refused certificate has expired
< \r\n~>
> +net wrong.zoraya:@TLSWRONG@ python3 https_client.py wrong.zoraya @TLSWRONG@\r
< refused
< \r\n~>
# The same server with no cafile: the default context finds the system roots
# (OPENSSLDIR/roots, /system/tls/roots), and with them only.
> +net test.zoraya:@TLSVALID@ python3 https_client.py test.zoraya @TLSVALID@ default\r
< status HTTP/1.1 200
< body Zoraya test page
< \r\n~>
# A blocking client (http.client, urllib: the file-descriptor BIO of patch 0001),
# no cafile: the valid server answers, the expired and wrong-name ones are
# refused before any request byte (the server's log is checked by the Makefile).
> +net test.zoraya:@TLSVALID@ python3 https_blocking.py test.zoraya @TLSVALID@ http.client\r
< status 200
< body Zoraya test page
< \r\n~>
> +net test.zoraya:@TLSVALID@ python3 https_blocking.py test.zoraya @TLSVALID@ urllib\r
